Options +FollowSymLinks
Options -MultiViews
RewriteEngine on

# ============================================================================
# MIME type registrations
# w3id mostly redirects (3xx) to GitHub raw, which sets its own Content-Type,
# so these are belt-and-braces - useful only if a representation is ever
# served directly from this host.
# ============================================================================
AddType application/rdf+xml      .rdf
AddType text/turtle              .ttl
AddType application/n-triples    .nt
AddType application/ld+json      .jsonld
AddType text/shex                .shex
AddType application/yaml         .yaml

# ============================================================================
# Minor caveats & accepted design trade-offs (deep-review notes)
# Every item below is minor (rare-in-practice) or trivial (cosmetic)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. [minor]   Conneg is regex-based and cannot parse `;q=` weights. First
#    matching rule wins by file order. Multi-Accept clients always get the
#    rule listed first (e.g. `Accept: application/json, text/turtle` ->
#    turtle). Rare: most clients send a single preferred type.
# 2. [trivial] Bare `<repo>/<anything>.yaml` always redirects to the
#    canonical schema YAML regardless of `<anything>` (LinkML schemas are
#    single-file; intentional).
# 3. [trivial] HTML conneg returns 303 (See Other); the LMODEL PROJECTS
#    catch-all returns 302 (Found). Same destination, different semantics
#    by design.
# 4. [trivial] `<repo>/jsonld/foo.json` and `<repo>/jsonschema/foo.json`
#    mis-route to `project/json/...`; honest 404 upstream either way.
#    Not worth guarding.
# 5. [trivial] `AddType` set is sparse - w3id.org always 3xx-redirects,
#    GitHub raw sets `Content-Type`. AddType only matters if served
#    directly here.
# 6. [trivial] Deprecated MIME variants (`text/x-yaml`, `application/x-
#    turtle`) not accepted by conneg; clients sending only those get 406.
# 7. [minor]   `[N,DPI]` rules assume single-pass aliasing (no alias-of-
#    alias). If chained aliases are added, order them so each `[N]` rule
#    precedes rules that match its output. Apache's LimitInternalRecursion
#    =10 cap applies.
# 8. [minor]   STEM override `^uco-([a-z0-9]+)(?:/|$)` matches only single-
#    segment subnames. Multi-hyphen repos (e.g. `nist-ai-rmf`) need an
#    explicit entry in the multi-hyphen block below.
# 9. [trivial] Repo segment `[^/]+` allows dots and unusual chars. No
#    security impact: every match feeds a fixed-template redirect URL
#    (no filesystem access, no traversal possible).
# 10. [trivial] `Options +FollowSymLinks` requires the host vhost to permit
#     it (w3id.org does). Not portable to restrictive shared hosts.
# ============================================================================

#### LMODEL ORGANIZATION ###

# Bare base URL -> GitHub organization page (information resource -> 302)
RewriteRule ^$ https://github.com/lmodel [R=302,L]

# ============================================================================
# Path canonicalization & aliases (internal rewrite, no client redirect).
#
# Apply *before* the conneg / artifact / schema rules so the entire pipeline
# sees the canonical form. The [N] flag re-runs the rewrite engine on the
# new URL; no infinite loops because each substitution removes the prefix
# the rule matches on.
# ============================================================================

# Legacy slash form -> canonical hyphen form.
# [DPI] (Discard PathInfo) prevents Apache from re-appending the original
# trailing path to the substitution result in per-directory context.
RewriteRule ^uco/([a-z0-9]+)((?:/.*)?)$ uco-$1$2 [N,DPI]
RewriteRule ^ucs/([a-z0-9]+)((?:/.*)?)$ ucs-$1$2 [N,DPI]

# nist-ai-600-1 (official NIST designation) -> nist-ai-rmf (publish slug).
# Full alias: docs, conneg, artifacts, schema all served from nist-ai-rmf.
RewriteRule ^nist-ai-600-1((?:/.*)?)$ nist-ai-rmf$1 [N,DPI]

# ============================================================================
# Filename-stem normalization & per-repo branch / layout overrides.
#
# gen-project converts hyphens in repo names to underscores in artifact
# stems (e.g., `uco-core` -> `uco_core.context.jsonld`). Apache `.htaccess`
# cannot translate hyphens to underscores natively (RewriteMap is forbidden
# in this context), so we set environment variables per request:
#
#   STEM      filename stem used in artifact names. Default: $1.
#   BRANCH    git branch the rules dereference. Default: main.
#             Typical values:
#               main       - default for lmodel-owned LinkML projects.
#               master     - upstream forks that never renamed (e.g. FINOS).
#               gh-pages   - CI-published artifact branch when project/ is
#                            gitignored on the source branch (see template
#                            below). Use this only if the deploy workflow
#                            commits gen-project output verbatim - the
#                            standard LinkML mkdocs deploy DOES NOT.
#               artifacts  - convention for a dedicated build branch.
#   PROJECT   path prefix under the branch where gen-project artifacts live,
#             with trailing slash. Default: "project/". Set to empty ("")
#             for repos whose artifacts live at the branch root (common
#             when using a dedicated artifacts branch).
#
# Rules below use %{ENV:STEM}, %{ENV:BRANCH}, %{ENV:PROJECT} where these
# values are needed; the GitHub repo segment in the redirect path
# continues to use $1 (the URL form).
#
# The default rule sets all three; subsequent specific rules override per
# repo. The `-` substitution leaves the URL unchanged and processing
# continues. Multiple [E=...] flags on a single rule set multiple vars at
# once.
#
# Reproducibility note: gen-project output is fully reproducible from
# `src/<stem>/schema/<stem>.yaml`. Repos may legitimately gitignore
# `project/` - in that case CI must publish the generated tree to a
# branch this rewriter can reach (raw.githubusercontent.com), and that
# repo gets a BRANCH override here. `.htaccess` only routes; it cannot
# regenerate missing artifacts.
#
# When adding a new lmodel repo whose name contains hyphens, add an entry
# below (single-hyphen subnames of uco-/ucs- are matched automatically).
# ============================================================================

# Defaults: STEM=URL repo segment, BRANCH=main, PROJECT=project/
RewriteRule ^([^/]+) - [E=STEM:$1,E=BRANCH:main,E=PROJECT:project/]

# UCO / UCS families: single hyphen after prefix, no internal hyphens.
RewriteRule ^uco-([a-z0-9]+)(?:/|$) - [E=STEM:uco_$1]
RewriteRule ^ucs-([a-z0-9]+)(?:/|$) - [E=STEM:ucs_$1]

# Multi-hyphen repos: enumerated (no regex shortcut available).
# Only repos that actually publish gen-project artifacts under the
# convention `src/<stem>/schema/<stem>.yaml` are listed. STEM is the
# hyphen->underscore form; BRANCH defaults to main and PROJECT to project/
# unless overridden on the same line.
# Excluded (fall through to docs catch-all only):
#   - sssom-files            : data repo, no LinkML schema
#   - linkml-project-copier  : Copier template, no LinkML schema
RewriteRule ^nist-sp-800-53(?:/|$)        - [E=STEM:nist_sp_800_53]
RewriteRule ^nist-sp-800-218(?:/|$)       - [E=STEM:nist_sp_800_218]
RewriteRule ^nist-sp-800-171(?:/|$)       - [E=STEM:nist_sp_800_171]
RewriteRule ^nist-csf-v2(?:/|$)           - [E=STEM:nist_csf_v2]
RewriteRule ^nist-ai-rmf(?:/|$)           - [E=STEM:nist_ai_rmf]
RewriteRule ^nist-nvd(?:/|$)              - [E=STEM:nist_nvd]
RewriteRule ^vulnerability-core(?:/|$)    - [E=STEM:vulnerability_core]
RewriteRule ^kev-catalog(?:/|$)           - [E=STEM:kev_catalog]
RewriteRule ^cis-controls(?:/|$)          - [E=STEM:cis_controls]
RewriteRule ^fluxnova-bpm-platform(?:/|$) - [E=STEM:fluxnova_bpm_platform]

# common-domain-model: FINOS upstream uses the `master` branch (no `main`).
# Schema YAML lives at the standard `src/<stem>/schema/<stem>.yaml` path on
# master; gen-project artifacts under `project/` must also be present on
# master for non-YAML conneg / extension routes to resolve.
RewriteRule ^common-domain-model(?:/|$)   - [E=STEM:common_domain_model,E=BRANCH:master]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Template: repo with `project/` gitignored, artifacts CI-published elsewhere
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Use one of these patterns when a repo intentionally does NOT commit its
# gen-project output to the source branch. The redirect target must be a
# branch that raw.githubusercontent.com can serve. Example variants:
#
#   # Variant A: artifacts pushed to a dedicated `artifacts` branch with
#   # the standard `project/<dir>/<stem>.<ext>` layout preserved.
#   #RewriteRule ^example-repo(?:/|$) - [E=STEM:example_repo,E=BRANCH:artifacts]
#
#   # Variant B: artifacts pushed to a branch with files at the branch root
#   # (no `project/` wrapper). Override PROJECT to empty.
#   #RewriteRule ^example-repo(?:/|$) - [E=STEM:example_repo,E=BRANCH:artifacts,E=PROJECT:]
#
#   # Variant C: artifacts living on `gh-pages` under `project/` (only
#   # works if the deploy workflow explicitly preserves the directory -
#   # mkdocs/material themes overwrite gh-pages root, so this requires a
#   # custom `mkdocs gh-deploy --remote-branch gh-pages --dirty` setup or
#   # a separate orphan branch).
#   #RewriteRule ^example-repo(?:/|$) - [E=STEM:example_repo,E=BRANCH:gh-pages]
#
# See TEST_REPORT.md for a worked smoke-test pattern. Activate by removing
# the leading `#` and testing the routes against the live repo.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ============================================================================
# Schemas - convenience routes to canonical YAML source.
# YAML schema is a Core LinkML representation of the model -> 303 See Other.
# Filename stem (%{ENV:STEM}) handles the hyphen->underscore convention
# of gen-project (see Filename-stem normalization block above).
#
# Three accepted forms:
#   <repo>/schema/<anything>.yaml   - explicit YAML extension
#   <repo>/schema[/<bare-name>]     - bare path under /schema/ (no extension)
#   <repo>/<anything>.yaml          - bare-extension fallback (excludes
#                                     prefixmap/golr/yaml/.linkml.yaml/schema
#                                     paths handled by other rules)
# All three resolve to src/<stem>/schema/<stem>.yaml. The third form
# always lands on the canonical schema regardless of the requested name -
# this is intentional (LinkML schemas are single-file).
# ============================================================================
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/schema/(.+)\.yaml$  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/src/%{ENV:STEM}/schema/%{ENV:STEM}.yaml [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/schema(?:/[^.]*)?$  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/src/%{ENV:STEM}/schema/%{ENV:STEM}.yaml [R=303,NE,L]

# Bare <repo>/<anything>.yaml fallback. Guards exclude paths claimed by
# more specific rules below (prefixmap, golr, yaml directory, .linkml.yaml).
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !/(schema|prefixmap|golr|yaml)/
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.linkml\.yaml$
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.yaml$         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/src/%{ENV:STEM}/schema/%{ENV:STEM}.yaml [R=303,NE,L]

# ============================================================================
# Core LinkML Artifacts - representations of the model (non-information
# resource) -> 303 See Other. All use [^/]+ for the repo segment to avoid
# greedy capture across nested paths.
# ============================================================================

# GraphQL
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.graphql$         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}graphql/$2.graphql [R=303,NE,L]

# JSON-LD (context + plain). The `.context.json` variant exists because some
# clients/CDNs reject `.jsonld` extension; the rewrite is identical.
# Bare `context.jsonld` (no prefix) is the common `@context` idiom - it must
# inject the repo's normalized stem (gen-project emits `<stem>.context.jsonld`).
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/context\.jsonld$      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonld/%{ENV:STEM}.context.jsonld [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/context\.json$        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonld/%{ENV:STEM}.context.jsonld [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.context\.jsonld$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonld/$2.context.jsonld [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.context\.json$   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonld/$2.context.jsonld [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.jsonld$         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonld/$2.jsonld [R=303,NE,L]

# JSON Schema + plain JSON. `.schema.json` is matched first; remaining `.json`
# requests fall through here. Excludes `/terminusdb/` (has its own Non-Core
# rule below that emits a different target directory).
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.schema\.json$  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonschema/$2.schema.json [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !/terminusdb/
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.json$          https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}json/$2.json [R=303,NE,L]

# OWL (gen-project emits as .owl.ttl), RDF/XML & N-Triples (from gen-rdf).
# Both `.owl` and `.owl.ttl` resolve to the same generated file, so a
# round-trip from the redirect target back to its filename works.
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.owl(?:\.ttl)?$   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}owl/$2.owl.ttl [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.rdf$             https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}rdf/$2.rdf [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.nt$              https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}rdf/$2.nt [R=303,NE,L]

# Prefix map (semantic config)
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/prefixmap/(.+)\.yaml$  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}prefixmap/$2.yaml [R=303,NE,L]

# Protobuf, SHACL, ShEx, SQL DDL.
# ShEx note: gen-shex emits .shex (compact) and .shexj (JSON). The
# .shexc extension is an alias for the compact form and resolves to the
# same .shex file.
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.proto$           https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}protobuf/$2.proto [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.shacl\.ttl$      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}shacl/$2.shacl.ttl [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.shex$            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}shex/$2.shex [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.shexc$           https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}shex/$2.shex [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.shexj$           https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}shex/$2.shexj [R=303,NE,L]
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !/sqlvalidation/
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.sql$             https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}sqlschema/$2.sql [R=303,NE,L]

# Turtle (excludes .owl.ttl which is matched by the .owl rule above)
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.owl\.
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.ttl$             https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}rdf/$2.ttl [R=303,NE,L]

# Merged LinkML YAML
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.linkml\.yaml$    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}linkml/$2.linkml.yaml [R=303,NE,L]

# ============================================================================
# Non-Core Artifacts - concrete information resources / code-gen outputs.
# Use 302 (cacheable). Not in scope for content negotiation: MIME types
# collide across path-segregated outputs (3× .py: pandera/sqla/namespaces;
# 3× .yaml: schema/golr/prefixmap; 2× .md: mermaid/markdown-datadict;
# 2× .sql: sqlschema/sqlvalidation) - only the URL path disambiguates.
# ============================================================================
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.xlsx$                  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}excel/$2.xlsx [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.java$                  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}java/$2.java [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.ts$                    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}typescript/$2.ts [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.h$                     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}cpp/$2.h [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.csv$                   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}csv/$2.csv [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.dbml$                  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}dbml/$2.dbml [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.er\.md$                https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}erdiagram/$2.er.md [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.go$                    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}golang/$2.go [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/golr/(.+)\.yaml$             https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}golr/$2.yaml [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.dot\.dot$              https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}graphviz/$2.dot.dot [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/markdown-datadict/(.+)\.md$  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}markdown-datadict/$2.md [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/mermaid/(.+)\.md$            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}mermaid/$2.md [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/namespaces/(.+)\.py$         https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}namespaces/$2.py [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/pandera/(.+)\.py$            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}pandera/$2.py [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.plantuml$              https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}plantuml/$2.plantuml [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/sqla/(.+)\.py$               https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}sqla/$2.py [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/sqlvalidation/(.+)\.sql$     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}sqlvalidation/$2.sql [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.sssom\.tsv$            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}sssom/$2.sssom.tsv [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/summary/(.+)\.tsv$           https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}summary/$2.tsv [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/terminusdb/(.+)\.json$       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}terminusdb/$2.json [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.tql$                   https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}typedb/$2.tql [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/yaml/(.+)\.yaml$             https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}yaml/$2.yaml [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/rust/Cargo\.toml$            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}rust/Cargo.toml [R=302,NE,L]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)/(.+)\.rq$                    https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}sparql/$2.rq [R=302,NE,L]

# ============================================================================
# Content negotiation - Core LinkML / Linked Data representations ONLY.
# Fires only when the request URI has no file extension (the client is
# asking for the model as an abstract resource and letting the server
# choose the representation). Each rule emits a single 303 See Other to
# the canonical raw artifact (or to the docs site for HTML).
#
# Scope: repo root AND any depth - so class/slot IRIs like
# /lmodel/<repo>/<TermName> also content-negotiate. The artifact filename
# stem comes from %{ENV:STEM} (see Filename-stem normalization block).
#
# Non-Core artifacts are intentionally excluded - see note above.
# ============================================================================

# Turtle
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/turtle [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}rdf/%{ENV:STEM}.ttl [R=303,NE,L]

# RDF/XML and OWL/XML (requires `gen-rdf` to have produced .rdf)
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/rdf\+xml [NC,OR]
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/owl\+xml [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}rdf/%{ENV:STEM}.rdf [R=303,NE,L]

# N-Triples
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/n-triples [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}rdf/%{ENV:STEM}.nt [R=303,NE,L]

# JSON-LD
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/ld\+json [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonld/%{ENV:STEM}.context.jsonld [R=303,NE,L]

# Plain JSON - fallback to JSON-LD context. Clients sending
# Accept: application/json (curl --json, generic HTTP libraries) get
# the JSON-LD @context document, the broadest sensible JSON form of
# the model. Must come AFTER application/ld+json so that clients
# accepting both pick the more specific representation.
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/json [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonld/%{ENV:STEM}.context.jsonld [R=303,NE,L]

# JSON Schema
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/schema\+json [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}jsonschema/%{ENV:STEM}.schema.json [R=303,NE,L]

# SHACL (Turtle profile)
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/shacl\+turtle [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}shacl/%{ENV:STEM}.shacl.ttl [R=303,NE,L]

# ShEx
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/shex [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/%{ENV:PROJECT}shex/%{ENV:STEM}.shex [R=303,NE,L]

# LinkML schema source (YAML)
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/yaml [NC,OR]
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/yaml [NC,OR]
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/x-yaml [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(?:/.*)?$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lmodel/$1/%{ENV:BRANCH}/src/%{ENV:STEM}/schema/%{ENV:STEM}.yaml [R=303,NE,L]

# HTML - browser default. Explicit `Accept: */*` (curl, libraries, crawlers
# without preference) is intentionally NOT matched here - it falls through
# to the LMODEL PROJECTS catch-all below, which redirects to the same docs
# site (R=302) and lets per-repo alias rules apply.
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} text/html [NC,OR]
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} application/xhtml\+xml [NC]
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(/.*)?$ https://lmodel.github.io/$1$2 [R=303,NE,L]

# 406 Not Acceptable - Accept header present, specific, and no representation
# matched. `Accept: */*` is explicitly excluded so generic clients fall
# through to the LMODEL PROJECTS catch-all instead of being rejected.
# Bare 406 (no body) per w3id convention for sites without a per-repo 406.html.
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !\.[^./]+$
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} .+
RewriteCond %{HTTP_ACCEPT} !\*/\*
RewriteRule ^(.+)$ - [R=406,L]

#### LMODEL PROJECTS ###
#
# All lmodel repos route generically - the catch-all below redirects any
# `<repo>/<rest>` path to `lmodel.github.io/<repo>/<rest>`.
#
# Aliases (slug A serves docs of slug B) and path canonicalization
# (e.g. `uco/core` -> `uco-core`) are applied as internal rewrites with
# `[N]` near the top of this file, so by the time we reach this section
# every request has its canonical `<repo>/<rest>` form.
#
# Earlier revisions of this file kept docs-site canonicalization rules
# for `uco-`, `ucs-`, and `nist-ai-600-1` here. Those rules were
# unreachable in normal operation (the `[N]` block already canonicalizes
# the path) and unhelpful as a fallback (artifact rules upstream of this
# section had already mis-routed by the time the canonicalization rules
# could fire). They have been removed; the catch-all below is sufficient.
RewriteRule ^([^/]+)(/.*)?$ https://lmodel.github.io/$1$2 [R=302,NE,L]
